<title>JAPAN: Key JGB yield falls to record low of 2.070 pct.</title>
<headline>Key JGB yield falls to record low of 2.070 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The yield of the key 182nd Japanese government bond (JGB) fell to a record low of 2.070 percent in late afternoon trade on Monday.</p>
<p>Traders said the decline in the key JGB yield was triggered by a fall in Tokyo share prices.  </p>
<p>The previous record low for any benchmark cash JGB yield was 2.075 percent, set on April 8.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-5473-3748</p>
